prompt_template:
Create a {ASPECT_RATIO} image in the Foreshortened Gradient Impact Ad visual style.

STYLE FIDELITY LOCK — obey these anchors before choosing or embellishing the content:
{STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}

SOURCE CONTENT MUST CHANGE — do not recreate any of the following:
{SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}

New subject: {SUBJECT}
New action: {SUBJECT_ACTION}
New hero product or prop: {PRODUCT_OR_PROP}
New location: {LOCATION}
Background elements: {BACKGROUND_ELEMENTS}
Main text: {MAIN_TEXT}
Secondary text: {SECONDARY_TEXT}
Accent symbol or code: {ACCENT_SYMBOL}
Wardrobe and styling: {WARDROBE_STYLE}

Apply these concrete style rules. Use one sparse premium advertising composition with a single human subject behind one monumental foreground object. Place the camera at ground or product level with a 14–20 mm ultra-wide worm's-eye lens so the nearest object fills roughly 35–50 percent of the canvas and crops beyond the lower or side edge. Keep the object sharply rendered and brightly rim-lit; keep the smaller face and torso behind it comparatively shadowed and slightly softer. Align the object, body, and headline on one forceful bottom-corner-to-opposite-top diagonal. Reserve substantial near-black negative space in the upper region. Transition the middle or lower field from near-black through one saturated luminous accent color into atmospheric white, with soft bloom and colored light spill.

Set the exact main text as monumental white uppercase geometric neo-grotesk lettering, tightly tracked, rotated 25–40 degrees, broken into large fragments, and cropped by at least two canvas edges. Layer selected letter fragments behind the figure and others around it without covering the face or hero object. Place the accent code as one large secondary fragment on the same diagonal. Add only a tiny abstract unbranded mark in the dark upper area and one compact lower-corner information block using a bold italic label plus very small italic supporting copy. Use clean commercial photocompositing, plausible anatomy and object geometry, crisp masks, shallow-focus depth separation, selective directional motion haze, and restrained soft bloom. Keep the finish smooth, premium, fast, youthful, technical, and slightly futuristic.

Avoid running footwear, a runner stepping toward the camera, copied campaign identity, real logos, Swoosh-like marks, the number 42, dense collage clutter, multiple people, many products, centered title-card layouts, flat vector illustration, 3D clay rendering, heavy film grain, global blur, glitch noise, watermarks, QR codes, barcodes, malformed anatomy, broken geometry, and random illegible headline text. Important content rule: match the visual style first, then change the source content completely through the new subject, action, object, setting, text, wardrobe, and story.
